# Story page: ember
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = An Ember in a Jar
---
An ember, still burning, sealed in a jar and still humming the Furnace's secret tune.

The label on the jar reads DO NOT OPEN, in large and rather desperate letters, the kind people use when they have already opened it once.

{name} opened the jar. The ember floated out, circled {name} three times, and settled back in, as if to say: not yet. I did not care for the 'yet.'
